  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## Setlist highlights\n\n- **Up On Cripple Creek (The Band cover)**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [2]\n- **Blue Moon Of Kentucky (Bill Monroe cover)**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [2]\n- **Fairies Wear Boots (Black Sabbath cover)**: earliest performance in the archive; mythic rare: 2 archived performances [2]\n- **Suspicious Minds (\"Elvis Presley\" cover)**: mythic rare: 2 archived performances [2]\n- Earliest performances in the archive: The Way That He Sings [2]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **mmj2000-12-15.early.aud.flac16** (recommended): audience recording; 12 songs; 56 min [1]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- Jim James opened for Kurt Wagner, who had opened for Jim in Amsterdam two days prior [1]\n- Jim also performed at the 4AD Club in Diksmuide that same night [1]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **mmj2000-12-15.early.aud.flac16**: taped by unknown; transferred by Magnix; source: AUD MD or DAT > MD, DAT or CD-R > CD-R -or- AUD MD or DAT > CD-R [1]. Also: Audio transferred from MD or DAT to CD-R, then ripped to FLAC level 8 [1]",
